WEBVTT

00:00:06.150 --> 00:00:09.320
I'd rather you not talk about that old man to Mytyl.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:12.860
Why? It's possible he's what we need to save her.

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:16.760
<i>Is it really possible, though?</i>

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.490
<i>She's afraid of that man.</i>

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:22.500
What is your wish?

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:26.830
I'm the god of this world,
so I'll grant any wish of yours.

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.760
If you're claiming to be the god, can you tell me
the difference between a god and a demon?

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:34.160
A god grants salvation and demands nothing.

00:00:34.160 --> 00:00:37.320
A demon grants power and demands your soul.

00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:42.100
But don't you take away their freedom
if they ask you to grant their wish?

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:43.940
I don't take anything from them.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.980
By being given one thing, you can lose another.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:52.520
If you're caught in a paradise granted
to you by a god and can't get out,

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:56.360
how is that any different
from your soul being stolen?

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:59.660
<i>Those are words that could destroy this Eden.</i>

00:01:02.630 --> 00:01:04.290
<i>It'll be time soon.</i>

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.510
I spent all day yesterday walking around the town.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:48.600
And today I heard from the Bureau
about Tyltyl and Mytyl.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.190
That's how I've more or less reached a conclusion.

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:52.980
Asai,

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:55.230
do you think this world is right?

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.280
I don't think it's right.

00:02:57.280 --> 00:03:00.610
But I don't think we have a say in it.

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.120
I hate this world.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:05.870
And I've been wondering why.

00:03:06.830 --> 00:03:09.370
I saw a poster long time ago.

00:03:09.370 --> 00:03:10.750
There was a picture

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:13.710
where everyone held hands
in a circle around the Earth.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:17.130
And in my heart, I felt that such things were right.

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:20.340
Katagiri Honoka is isolated from people.

00:03:20.340 --> 00:03:22.640
The way she secludes herself in her own world

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.600
and creates her own god
is what you find problematic, isn't it?

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:30.600
In my heart, I feel that such a thing is disgusting.

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:34.020
This world is all Katagiri has.

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:37.360
If she can't wake up in reality,
this is her only way to be happy.

00:03:37.360 --> 00:03:38.780
You've got me wrong.

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:41.860
I'm not against the ability
to create a world inside a dream.

00:03:41.860 --> 00:03:45.120
The problem is creating Tyltyl and becoming Mytyl.

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:47.240
That is warped and disgusting.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.910
I don't know

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.620
if this case should be solved high-handedly, though.

00:03:51.620 --> 00:03:52.790
But I know.

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:55.380
This world wants to be saved.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.340
Why do you think so?

00:03:57.340 --> 00:03:59.880
It's the only reason a monster
would destroy the town.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:04.890
The truth is that Katagiri Honoka, who created
this world, also hates it, or at least I think so.

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:06.430
Please wait!

00:04:06.430 --> 00:04:07.850
I won't.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:10.520
I'm going to fix this world.

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:12.560
I'll destroy it and return it to a blank state.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.440
And what good will that do?

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:18.820
Won't Mytyl remember that she's Katagiri Honoka?

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:22.320
Then she can start over and create a proper world.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:25.950
Ukawa, I respect your strength.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.910
But I've never once thought you were righteous.

00:04:28.910 --> 00:04:30.160
If I had to compare...

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.120
I've never once thought you're
a better person than Haruki Misora.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:36.960
Asai, I really hate to say this,

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:41.630
but I strongly believe my sense
of what is right is better than yours.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:00.690
You're reckless, Ukawa.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:03.650
What happened to people
who were in tall buildings?

00:05:03.650 --> 00:05:05.070
They'll be fine.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:08.410
Getting hurt inside a dream
doesn't affect your real self.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:11.080
What just happened?

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:14.710
Ukawa erased all the buildings.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.500
That's absurd.

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.670
Ukawa has an ability that can alter a world.

00:05:20.170 --> 00:05:22.760
She can do anything she imagines
as long as it doesn't affect living beings.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:29.010
You sure erased everything nicely.

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:32.560
I did, including the written copy of the Script.

00:05:32.850 --> 00:05:34.430
Is that a problem?

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.190
It'd have been better if you'd waited a bit longer...

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:38.150
Doesn't matter.

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:42.570
I wish you'd left at least a bed to sleep
in for when we want to go back.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:56.710
Hi, morning.

00:06:01.380 --> 00:06:03.800
Could you place a lock on this?

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:09.890
If you used Kagaya's ability on me,

00:06:09.890 --> 00:06:12.510
would I not get affected by resets?

00:06:12.510 --> 00:06:16.480
I don't want to lose my memories of today, if possible.

00:06:16.480 --> 00:06:21.110
Generally, using his ability on people is forbidden.

00:06:24.280 --> 00:06:25.530
I see.

00:06:28.450 --> 00:06:31.070
Do you hate that dream world?

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:34.870
It reminds me of something I absolutely hate.

00:06:34.870 --> 00:06:35.910
Which is?

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:38.710
This place.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:41.080
It reminds me of the real Sakurada.

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.210
One Hand Eden, a paradise of easy life.

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:49.180
Reminds me of this strange town, full of abilities
that let you achieve results just by wishing for them.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.510
You sure hate abilities.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.140
It's not as much hate as fear.

00:06:54.140 --> 00:06:59.100
There's no way I could approve of an individual
possessing a power that could destroy the world.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:04.480
The nameless system verified that
Ukawa Sasane is harmless, though.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:10.200
And who'll verify if the nameless system is correct?

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:14.830
You hate your own ability, am I wrong?

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.790
The ability to completely see
through the feelings of others.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.080
Is something wrong with that?

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.170
This is where your value lies, in my opinion.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:26.920
Ability users are supposed to hate their abilities.

00:07:30.680 --> 00:07:33.550
It's as though the world ended.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:36.180
I have a hypothesis.

00:07:36.510 --> 00:07:39.810
The real hospital is at the east end of Sakurada,

00:07:39.810 --> 00:07:43.810
but in the dream world, east and west are reversed, so it's at the west end.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:47.980
I've been thinking about
why it's like that all this time.

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:50.240
Have you reached an answer?

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:56.490
My theory is that the directions
might not be reversed at all, actually.

00:07:56.490 --> 00:08:00.160
We might be out above the sea right now.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:04.130
In that case, I might know what's
on the other side of this wall.

00:08:04.130 --> 00:08:07.800
The dream world's real Sakurada?

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:09.380
It'd all make sense that way.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:13.760
This was probably a replica
of the town that Tyltyl made.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:15.340
What are you going to do?

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.270
Tyltyl! I want to meet you!

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.100
Could you let us through?

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.880
It really was here.

00:09:00.220 --> 00:09:01.600
Are we getting on?

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:02.930
Of course.

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.370
Is that the god?

00:09:27.370 --> 00:09:28.580
I wonder.

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.800
Welcome. I've been waiting for you.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:43.060
Are you the god of this world?

00:09:43.060 --> 00:09:45.390
Yes, I'm Tyltyl.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:49.400
I was created as the false god of this world.

00:09:51.110 --> 00:09:51.900
Here.

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.530
If we're going to talk, you should sit down.

00:09:57.200 --> 00:09:57.950
Haruki!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.500
Beautiful.

00:10:14.710 --> 00:10:18.180
Do you mind if I visit you in the hospital in reality?

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:20.510
I want to meet you again.

00:10:20.510 --> 00:10:21.760
That's impossible.

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:25.220
No one is allowed to visit me in the hospital.

00:10:25.220 --> 00:10:27.390
The Bureau decided so.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:30.980
You should just forget about me and live on.

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:33.480
And what are you going to do?

00:10:33.480 --> 00:10:35.320
I'm not going to do anything.

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:38.740
As long as this world stays the same,

00:10:38.740 --> 00:10:41.450
I'll spend my days alone here watching the sky.

00:10:42.990 --> 00:10:45.740
What do you think will happen to this world?

00:10:45.740 --> 00:10:47.040
Who knows.

00:10:47.040 --> 00:10:49.250
It's for the god to decide.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:54.460
Why did you confine yourself in your
office and keep using your ability?

00:10:54.460 --> 00:10:56.380
It was comfortable.

00:10:56.760 --> 00:11:01.640
It was comfortable to spend my life
looking at the truth in solitude.

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:03.970
Were you happy like that?

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:08.480
Yes, solitude brings me happiness.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.490
Where is Kei?

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:20.530
You're not in danger.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:21.780
Don't worry about it.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:23.280
Please tell me.

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.620
He's somewhere you can't reach on your own.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.080
Don't worry, you'll meet him again soon.

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:29.290
You can sit down for now.

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:36.130
Welcome to the dream world.

00:11:36.130 --> 00:11:39.010
Here you can have anything you wish for.

00:11:39.510 --> 00:11:42.300
Now, tell me what your wish is.

00:11:42.300 --> 00:11:44.220
I do not have any.

00:11:44.970 --> 00:11:48.060
You're strongly bound by a certain young man.

00:11:48.850 --> 00:11:49.810
That's true.

00:11:49.810 --> 00:11:52.270
And being bound by that young man,

00:11:52.270 --> 00:11:55.400
your simple self has become
so much more complicated.

00:11:55.400 --> 00:11:56.820
I do not understand.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:12:03.240
Without you realizing, your real self
has diverged from how he defines you.

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:05.820
The truth is that you have a lot you'd wish for,

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:09.580
but you started hiding
behind a mask of selflessness.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:13.210
You have two selves that contradict each other.

00:12:13.830 --> 00:12:18.460
I know a spell that'll awaken the other you, though.

00:12:19.510 --> 00:12:20.590
Let's try it.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.180
If you don't do anything,

00:12:24.180 --> 00:12:27.850
Souma Sumire might end up taking away Asai Kei.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.930
Asai Kei will long for Souma Sumire,

00:12:31.930 --> 00:12:34.600
and won't even turn your way.

00:12:38.190 --> 00:12:40.570
You should take your time talking this through

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:44.280
with your other self, who knows what you wish for.

00:12:46.990 --> 00:12:49.660
You hate me.

00:12:49.660 --> 00:12:51.910
But that's a contradiction.

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:54.670
Since you don't really have anything,

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.750
you shouldn't be able to hate anyone.

00:12:58.670 --> 00:13:00.550
What have you done?

00:13:00.550 --> 00:13:03.300
I sent Haruki Misora to see another me.

00:13:03.630 --> 00:13:05.220
Another you?

00:13:05.220 --> 00:13:06.760
Come on, sit down.

00:13:07.300 --> 00:13:09.890
Welcome to the dream world.

00:13:09.890 --> 00:13:13.020
Here you can have anything you wish for.

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:15.230
What is your wish?

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:17.480
I have two things I'd like to ask you for.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.110
That's pretty greedy.

00:13:19.110 --> 00:13:23.280
First, please let me read volume 407 of the Script.

00:13:23.570 --> 00:13:26.490
That's not your wish, is it?

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:28.410
My dear Sumire told you to do so.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:30.870
You know Souma Sumire?

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:34.040
She's the only friend I have.

00:13:34.290 --> 00:13:37.330
So what's your second wish?

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:41.960
I want to know what'll happen
if Souma Sumire leaves Sakurada.

00:13:41.960 --> 00:13:45.010
Could you let me test that here, in the dream world?

00:13:46.300 --> 00:13:47.720
Specifically,

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:51.010
I first want you to get help from a girl called Oka Eri,

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:53.930
and rewrite Souma's parents' memories.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:58.560
Make them forget that Souma died two years ago,
and move their house out of Sakurada.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:13:59.940
Would that be possible?

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:02.360
Of course it is.

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:05.650
But to me, this world is my reality.

00:14:05.650 --> 00:14:07.280
Yeah, I guess so.

00:14:07.280 --> 00:14:08.990
You should understand then.

00:14:08.990 --> 00:14:12.200
You can't use the people
of this world as guinea pigs.

00:14:12.200 --> 00:14:13.830
That's not true.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:17.040
I know that you're actually sacrificing
a whole town's worth of people.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.380
I need you to do the same thing for me.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:27.930
Tyltyl,

00:14:27.930 --> 00:14:30.390
if this world is important to you,

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:33.720
why are you letting a monster run wild?

00:14:34.970 --> 00:14:37.480
Was it Mytyl who created it?

00:14:37.480 --> 00:14:39.230
Is there something wrong with that?

00:14:39.230 --> 00:14:40.270
Indeed.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:42.860
I've finally learned the truth about this world.

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.820
You know nothing!

00:14:45.780 --> 00:14:48.320
It's not just Mytyl that is Katagiri Honoka.

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.620
This whole world is her.

00:14:54.080 --> 00:14:55.830
Why do you hate me?

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.460
You're worthless to Kei.

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:02.960
<i>So I'm not as polite when I talk with myself...</i>

00:15:02.960 --> 00:15:06.130
But I was created from within you.

00:15:06.130 --> 00:15:09.720
Essentially, you wanted me to exist.

00:15:09.720 --> 00:15:13.720
You didn't actually want
Souma Sumire to be born again.

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:15.930
Because with Souma Sumire's future-seeing

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:18.560
your reset ability would lose its value to Kei.

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:20.100
You were afraid of that.

00:15:20.100 --> 00:15:21.400
Yeah.

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:23.610
But it doesn't matter anymore.

00:15:23.610 --> 00:15:26.480
Kei chose to revive her, so I follow him.

00:15:26.860 --> 00:15:30.490
When Kei decided to take
Souma Sumire outside of Sakurada,

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:32.700
it made you happy.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:35.120
Because your reset ability will remain useful.

00:15:35.120 --> 00:15:37.330
This isn't about me.

00:15:37.330 --> 00:15:39.750
If Kei chose so, I approve of it.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.420
But I don't like that.

00:15:42.960 --> 00:15:46.420
It might be better for Souma Sumire
to remain in Sakurada.

00:15:47.750 --> 00:15:48.920
Why?

00:15:48.920 --> 00:15:53.140
I'm sure that Kei wants to be with Souma Sumire.

00:15:53.140 --> 00:15:56.810
And since I genuinely wish for Asai Kei's happiness,

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.770
the right thing to do might
be to keep Souma Sumire here.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:04.440
What you actually hate,

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:07.480
what you actually fear deep in your heart

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:13.740
is the possibility that you yourself might not be
prioritizing Asai Kei's happiness over anything else.

00:16:13.740 --> 00:16:17.200
This emotion of wanting to monopolize him

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:19.240
is what you very emotionally hate.

00:16:19.950 --> 00:16:23.000
Both me and you are emotions.

00:16:23.500 --> 00:16:27.040
You were in your little Eden.

00:16:27.040 --> 00:16:30.420
You were protecting yourself
in a very easy to live place.

00:16:31.510 --> 00:16:33.430
Now, tell me.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:36.350
Tell me what your wish is.

00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:41.600
Tyltyl,

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:45.100
I finally understand what I myself wish for.

00:16:45.100 --> 00:16:46.650
What is it?

00:16:46.650 --> 00:16:48.270
I want to grow.

00:16:48.690 --> 00:16:53.150
I want to be of greater value
than anyone or anything else to Kei.

00:16:53.490 --> 00:16:57.570
That's why I have nothing to ask you for, Tyltyl.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.040
I see.

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.870
Now I know why there is a monster.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.830
Mytyl wishes for it.

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:08.290
Why do you think so?

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:11.800
If nothing attacked, she wouldn't need to be protected.

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.630
Mytyl wants to be protected, am I wrong?

00:17:16.010 --> 00:17:17.390
No, you're not.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:20.810
Mytyl... Katagiri Honoka is lonely.

00:17:20.810 --> 00:17:26.230
Her ability was originally only
to talk with people inside a dream.

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:30.320
She just wanted a connection with
people who were sleeping next to her.

00:17:30.900 --> 00:17:33.360
But the Bureau has taken away even that from her,

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:35.820
and she became truly lonely, all alone.

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:41.240
And having lost all connection with people,
Katagiri created a god and an enemy.

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:42.290
That's right.

00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:46.830
The monster and I were born,
and she became Mytyl, unaware of anything.

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:50.340
Do you think this world is wrong?

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:52.380
It's definitely not right.

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:54.210
The means and the end don't match at all.

00:17:54.880 --> 00:17:59.930
You can't create both the hero and the villain
yourself if you want to connect with people.

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.350
In the end, she's still all alone.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:06.270
She keeps claiming this place is Eden.

00:18:06.270 --> 00:18:10.610
And yet, somewhere deep
in her heart, she knows it's a lie.

00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:15.440
As much as she might pretend to have
forgotten everything, she's aware of her solitude.

00:18:16.070 --> 00:18:18.360
You love her.

00:18:18.950 --> 00:18:20.530
Of course.

00:18:20.530 --> 00:18:23.160
I was created to.

00:18:23.160 --> 00:18:26.370
That's why I can't save Mytyl.

00:18:27.160 --> 00:18:29.750
I can't erase her solitude.

00:18:29.750 --> 00:18:34.090
I'm never able to do the one thing I was born for.

00:18:34.630 --> 00:18:39.220
That's why you created the reversed Sakurada.

00:18:39.220 --> 00:18:42.640
You knew that place would be destroyed by Ukawa.

00:18:43.510 --> 00:18:45.180
Did Souma tell you?

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:49.730
Mytyl is currently crying in that destroyed town.

00:18:49.730 --> 00:18:53.900
She doesn't understand why
I'm not coming to her rescue,

00:18:53.900 --> 00:18:56.190
and so she's crying in her loneliness.

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:58.860
Once her tears run dry, she'll think.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:01.160
What can she do to end her loneliness?

00:19:01.160 --> 00:19:04.490
Where is the Eden that has
been protecting her all this time?

00:19:04.910 --> 00:19:09.750
Mytyl knows nothing outside of that
little town surrounded by a white wall.

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:11.120
But Katagiri Honoka

00:19:11.580 --> 00:19:14.250
knows that this world is far bigger than that.

00:19:15.130 --> 00:19:18.920
Once Mytyl regains all of
Katagiri Honoka's memories,

00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:21.340
she'll step outside that wall, right?

00:19:21.340 --> 00:19:24.100
I want to believe that she will.

00:19:24.100 --> 00:19:26.100
Will that save Mytyl?

00:19:26.890 --> 00:19:28.020
I don't know.

00:19:28.350 --> 00:19:31.100
But she can't stay the way she is now.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:33.520
This world is a little bit too sad.

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:35.070
Tyltyl,

00:19:35.070 --> 00:19:37.320
I can't become a god.

00:19:37.320 --> 00:19:40.530
But I might be able to help Mytyl
make some friends at least.

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:43.820
I might not be able to do much,

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:47.120
but I'll try to make this world her real Eden.

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.870
That's why I ask of you, Tyltyl.

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:52.210
Will you help me with my experiment?

00:19:54.630 --> 00:19:56.550
I get it. I will.

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:01.220
Even I want to grant someone's wish at least once.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:15.520
<i>Volume 407 of the Script...</i>

00:20:17.900 --> 00:20:20.150
<i>Sakurada... abilities...</i>

00:20:20.530 --> 00:20:21.780
<i>The Bureau...</i>

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:24.280
<i>"The first year..."</i>

00:20:24.280 --> 00:20:26.910
<i>I'm sure this is what Souma wanted me to know.</i>

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:27.620
Kei.

00:20:29.740 --> 00:20:31.620
Hey, where have you been?

00:20:33.000 --> 00:20:34.790
I was meeting Tyltyl.

00:20:34.790 --> 00:20:36.540
I see. Did anything happen?

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:39.340
Tyltyl asked me if I had any wishes,

00:20:39.340 --> 00:20:41.920
and I answered that I have none.

00:20:41.920 --> 00:20:43.680
What were you doing?

00:20:44.050 --> 00:20:45.640
The same as you.

00:20:45.640 --> 00:20:47.800
Tyltyl asked me what I wished for as well.

00:20:47.800 --> 00:20:49.810
Did you ask him for anything?

00:20:49.810 --> 00:20:51.060
I did.

00:20:51.060 --> 00:20:53.810
He promised he'll help us test Souma's case.

00:20:54.100 --> 00:20:56.980
In return, I'll resolve Mytyl's problem.

00:20:56.980 --> 00:20:58.440
Mytyl's problem?

00:20:58.770 --> 00:21:02.740
It seems that this whole world is Katagiri Honoka.

00:21:02.740 --> 00:21:07.240
So someone forcefully destroying all of it,
even if it's because this world isn't right,

00:21:07.240 --> 00:21:09.080
is something I can't approve of.

00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:19.540
What is that?

00:21:19.540 --> 00:21:21.250
That's Katagiri Honoka.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:23.880
She wants to open her eyes.

00:21:23.880 --> 00:21:26.510
That's why the monster has so many of them.

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:28.850
She wants someone to take her hand,

00:21:28.850 --> 00:21:31.260
which is why it has so many of them.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:35.270
She's all alone, lonely, so scared
that it makes her scream inside,

00:21:35.270 --> 00:21:36.650
and so it does aloud.

00:21:38.310 --> 00:21:41.900
To summarize, I'd say that the monster
is Katagiri Honoka's very emotions.

00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.150
What is it doing?

00:21:44.150 --> 00:21:46.360
It's looking for the blue bird.

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:50.910
But it can't find the blue bird this way.

00:21:55.000 --> 00:21:56.500
Next Episode

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:59.540
The future I see isn't absolute.

00:21:59.540 --> 00:22:00.540
What are you plotting?

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:02.460
It's been a while, Souma Sumire.

00:22:02.460 --> 00:22:03.670
I can't save you.

00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:05.260
It's fine. You're not alone anymore!

00:22:05.260 --> 00:22:08.510
Please... save me!

00:22:16.430 --> 00:22:20.400
On such a cold dark sky of grey

00:22:22.690 --> 00:22:26.610
Rises the sun, which breathes life into it

00:22:28.740 --> 00:22:32.870
A scenery so plain and so mundane

00:22:33.160 --> 00:22:42.460
And yet it seems to break my heart, it's so dear to me

00:22:43.340 --> 00:22:46.920
As the time never stops passing by

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:49.300
You get lost while searching for

00:22:49.300 --> 00:22:53.180
Pure like the rays of a morning star

00:22:53.180 --> 00:22:56.100
What we all yearn for the most

00:22:56.100 --> 00:22:59.060
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:22:59.060 --> 00:22:59.520
In what colors bliss is dyed

00:22:59.640 --> 00:23:02.150
Struggling against all your past mistakes

00:23:02.150 --> 00:23:05.190
At last from the answer you found kindness fills your heart

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:08.360
More beautiful than anything you know

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:11.990
And you find it behind a dark veil of sadness

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:14.490
If I closed my eyes and stopped my thoughts

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:16.240
If it were so simple to just

00:23:16.240 --> 00:23:19.250
Lock your own heart

00:23:19.250 --> 00:23:22.380
How lovely life would be

00:23:22.380 --> 00:23:27.630
But I believe you have the key

00:23:28.420 --> 00:23:33.970
To let my soul be free
